-- one layout, each shape the notation can read
ok   day first            
ok   month first          
ok   a short month name   
ok   long names, and a day
ok   no separators        
ok   a full timestamp     
ok   12-hour, pm          
ok   12-hour, midnight    
ok   12-hour, noon        
ok   a time only          

-- a two-digit year takes the POSIX pivot: 00-68 this century, 69-99 the last
ok   26 is 2026           
ok   68 is 2068           
ok   69 is 1969           
ok   99 is 1999           

-- A LIST, AND THE ORDER IS THE DECLARATION
ok   dmy declared first   
ok   mdy declared first   
ok   and they DIFFER      

-- and the list disambiguates itself where the data allows
ok   03/15 can only be mdy
ok   15/03 can only be dmy
ok   the third candidate  

-- refusals, each beside a legal neighbour
ok   a contradictory day  
ok   names the text       
ok   and both layouts     
ok   day 32               
ok   trailing text        
ok   text too short       
ok   hour 13 with pm      
ok   a non-text subject   

-- A DAY THAT DOES NOT EXIST IN THAT MONTH
ok   29 Feb in a non-leap 
ok   30 Feb ever          
ok   31 April             
ok   31 June via a layout 
ok   CONTROL 2024 leap    
ok   CONTROL 2000 leap    
ok   1900 is NOT leap     
ok   CONTROL 28 Feb       
ok   CONTROL 30 April     
ok   CONTROL 31 December  

-- CONTROLS: the no-argument forms are untouched
ok   {date} ISO           
ok   {datetime} ISO and Z 
ok   {time} ISO           
ok   read then render     
ok   and the long way     
